From: EglantinePS5
Subject: up: kept translations survive a reinstall and a build that did not change the translator (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP), off by default

What: the kept-translation store (EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP) and the converted shader set are
stamped with the eboot's size and write time, so every install and every build starts them cold.
With EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP=1, when EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_EXE is unset and the build
carries a translation id, that field becomes src<32 hex> (SHA-256 of the translator as compiled:
src/shader_recompiler/** with every quoted include it reaches, the per-pipeline inputs
(_cost.cpp, the rewritten shader_environment.cpp, vk_pipeline_prep, vk_pipeline_cache.h,
pipeline_helper.h, fixed_pipeline_state, maxwell_to_vk, surface, transform_feedback), sirit, the
SPIR-V headers, the compiler and flags; made at build time by tools/gen-translation-id.py, wrapper
side) plus dev<16 hex> (CityHash64 of every field of Shader::Profile and HostTranslateInfo and four
device answers: transform feedback, MoltenVK, tessellation, max patch size; static_asserts and
t138/check/check-core.py keep the lists whole), and EDEN_NX2_TRANSCODE_WAIT and
EDEN_NX2_PRELOAD_ALL_PIPELINES (scheduling only) leave the switch hash. Without the id, or with
the switch off, the stamp is today's string byte for byte.

Safety net: the boot comparison, the 48 probes and EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_VERIFY stay. New: on the
first boot after the installed build changed under a reused store (sidecar prep_<hash>.build,
evicted with the store), up to EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP_PROBES (256) kept records, not 1
in 8, are translated afresh with no stage cache and their SPIR-V and infos compared; any
difference resets the whole store (the existing reset). A refused or failed probe is no
difference. The sidecar is written only when the check is done (not stopped; on a crossing boot
only when at least one probe was made). Lines: "EDEN_UP_SHADER_PREP_SOURCE_STAMP: id src... (files
N) dev..., store prep_xxxxxxxx reused|new (N pipelines), build <eboot>" and "...: store
reused|new|reset, crossed build yes|no, probes P (up to N, ...)".

Off: the stamp, the store name and the probes are T137's; the device digest is not made and the
installed build is not looked up (CurrentBuild runs only in source mode).

Build step (wrapper side, headless/vulkan.cmake): the context file is written by file(GENERATE)
for the CXX evaluation only (CONDITION $<COMPILE_LANGUAGE:CXX>); the target options carry
per-language parts, and one text per language failed the CMake generate step (13 Nov).

Credits: the mechanism, the switch names and the 0926 list are waveydude's (patches 0925 and 0926,
fork waveydude/Eglantine-PS5-, branch w11-two-frame-guard, commits 2ca0fdb and 07a1fb0); off by
default, fail-closed fallback and the Info+SPIR-V compare from our earlier drafts; two reviews
found the gaps our notes (12 Nov) answer.
